      "message": "I added `IsOkayToCreateInternalResources` as a generic flag to be used for any similar issues where the dawn front end is doing work we can\u0027t do while capturing.\n\nI could instead try to turn off the existing `Toggle::DisableTimestampQueryConversion`. Something like this\n\n```cpp\n// in DeviceWGPU.cpp\n\nnamespace {\n\nTogglesState PrepTogglesForDeviceWGPU(const TogglesState\u0026 toggles) {\n    TogglesState result(toggles);\n    result.ForceSet(Toggle::DisableTimestampQueryConversion, false);\n    return result;\n}\n\n} // namespace\n\nDevice::Device(AdapterBase* adapter,\n               WGPUAdapter innerAdapter,\n               const UnpackedPtr\u003cDeviceDescriptor\u003e\u0026 descriptor,\n               const TogglesState\u0026 deviceToggles,\n               Ref\u003cDeviceBase::DeviceLostEvent\u003e\u0026\u0026 lostEvent)\n    : DeviceBase(adapter, descriptor, PrepTogglesForDeviceWGPU(deviceToggles), std::move(lostEvent)),\n      ObjectWGPU(ToBackend(adapter-\u003eGetPhysicalDevice())-\u003eGetFunctions().deviceRelease),\n      wgpu(ToBackend(adapter-\u003eGetPhysicalDevice())-\u003eGetFunctions()) {\n\n```\n\nI thought the generic flag might be more useful but can switch it.",
